Resumed sessions replay the user content as it was sent

The transcript records a user prompt before the per-turn reminders are added
(current date, plan mode, output style, memory recall, IDE context), so
--continue and session resume rebuilt each earlier turn without them. The
restored prompt then differed from the live one early in the first user
message, and a provider prompt cache could reuse only the system prompt and
tools. The client now also records the user content of a UserQuery or Cron
turn as it went out (system record `sent_user_content`; parts unchanged from
the user record are stored as references, so images are not stored twice),
and the history rebuild puts those parts back in place of the recorded
request. The memory catalog stays request-only, as before. Tool-result turns
are not covered.

